@page "/accessibility/focus-trap"
@namespace CymruBlazor.Demo.Pages.Components.Accessibility
@inject IFocusManager FocusManager

<div class="cb-page-header">
    <h1 class="cb-page-title">FocusTrap</h1>
    <a class="cb-open-in-github"
       href="https://github.com/gncube/CymruBlazor/blob/main/src/CymruBlazor/Components/Accessibility/CyFocusTrap.razor"
       target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open in GitHub<span class="u-sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>
    <p class="cb-page-description">
        A wrapper that asks an <code>IFocusManager</code> to move focus into its
        content on first render and to restore focus when it is removed. The
        focus manager registered by default only logs those requests, so today
        this component does not move, restore or contain focus. A working
        implementation is planned for 1.3.0.
    </p>
</div>

<CyAlert Severity="ComponentColour.Warning" Title="Preview: focus movement and containment are not implemented yet">
    <p style="margin:0">
        <code>CyFocusTrap</code> currently renders a <code>&lt;div tabindex="-1"&gt;</code> and
        calls <code>IFocusManager</code>. The default <code>FocusManager</code> logs at Debug
        level and returns success without touching the page: focus does not move on open,
        <kbd>Tab</kbd> can leave the panel, and focus is not restored on close. Do not rely on
        it to build a modal dialog. You can register your own <code>IFocusManager</code>
        (see below).
    </p>
</CyAlert>

<div class="cb-section">
    <h2 class="cb-section-title">Basic usage</h2>
    <p class="cb-section-description">
        When <code>Enabled</code> is <code>true</code> (the default) and
        <code>AutoFocus</code> is <code>true</code>, the trap asks the
        <code>IFocusManager</code> to focus its container after the first render.
        With the default focus manager nothing visibly happens: try pressing
        <kbd>Tab</kbd> in the demo panel to see focus leave it.
    </p>

    <div class="cb-example">
        <span class="cb-example__label">Interactive</span>
        <div class="cb-example__preview">
            @if (!_trapVisible)
            {
                <button id="open-trap-btn"
                        class="cb-demo-btn"
                        @onclick="OpenTrap">
                    Open focus trap panel
                </button>
            }
            else
            {
                <CyFocusTrap Enabled="true"
                           AutoFocus="true"
                           RestoreFocus="true"
                           Style="display:block;padding:var(--cymru-space-6);
                                  border:2px solid var(--cymru-color-primary);
                                  border-radius:var(--cymru-radius-md);
                                  background:var(--cymru-color-surface)">
                    <CyStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="ComponentSize.Medium">
                        <p style="margin:0;font-weight:600">This panel is wrapped in a CyFocusTrap.</p>
                        <p style="margin:0;font-size:var(--cymru-font-size-sm);
                                  color:var(--cymru-color-text-muted)">
                            With the default focus manager, Tab is not contained here.
                        </p>
                        <input type="text"
                               placeholder="First focusable element"
                               style="padding:var(--cymru-space-2);
                                      border:1px solid var(--cymru-color-border);
                                      border-radius:var(--cymru-radius-sm);
                                      width:100%;box-sizing:border-box" />
                        <input type="text"
                               placeholder="Second focusable element"
                               style="padding:var(--cymru-space-2);
                                      border:1px solid var(--cymru-color-border);
                                      border-radius:var(--cymru-radius-sm);
                                      width:100%;box-sizing:border-box" />
                        <button class="cb-demo-btn cb-demo-btn--secondary"
                                @onclick="CloseTrap">
                            Close panel
                        </button>
                    </CyStack>
                </CyFocusTrap>
            }
        </div>
        <pre class="cb-example__code"><code>&lt;CyFocusTrap Enabled="true"
             AutoFocus="true"
             RestoreFocus="true"&gt;
    &lt;input type="text" /&gt;
    &lt;button @@onclick="Close"&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/CyFocusTrap&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="cb-section">
    <h2 class="cb-section-title">Disabled trap</h2>
    <p class="cb-section-description">
        Set <code>Enabled="false"</code> to render the wrapper without asking the
        focus manager to do anything on first render.
    </p>
    <pre><code>&lt;CyFocusTrap Enabled="@@_isOpen"&gt;
    ...
&lt;/CyFocusTrap&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="cb-section">
    <h2 class="cb-section-title">Providing your own focus manager</h2>
    <p class="cb-section-description">
        <code>CyFocusTrap</code> calls whatever <code>IFocusManager</code> is registered.
        <code>AddCymruBlazor()</code> registers a logging placeholder; register your own
        afterwards (the last registration wins) to move and restore focus for real, for
        example through JavaScript interop.
    </p>
    <pre><code>builder.Services.AddCymruBlazor();
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IFocusManager, MyJsFocusManager&gt;();</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="cb-section">
    <h2 class="cb-section-title">API</h2>
    <table class="cb-api-table" aria-label="FocusTrap parameters">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Parameter</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Default</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td class="cb-api-table__name">Enabled</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__type">bool</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__default">true</td>
                <td>When false, no focus request is made on first render</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="cb-api-table__name">AutoFocus</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__type">bool</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__default">true</td>
                <td>Asks the focus manager to focus the container on first render (no effect with the default manager)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="cb-api-table__name">RestoreFocus</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__type">bool</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__default">true</td>
                <td>Asks the focus manager to restore the previously focused element on disposal (no effect with the default manager)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="cb-api-table__name">ChildContent</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__type">RenderFragment</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__default">—</td>
                <td>Content rendered inside the trap container</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="cb-api-table__name">Class</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__type">string?</td>
                <td class="cb-api-table__default">null</td>
                <td>Additional CSS classes on the root <code>&lt;div&gt;</code></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="cb-section">
    <h2 class="cb-section-title">Accessibility notes</h2>
    <ul style="color:var(--cymru-color-text);line-height:1.75;
               padding-inline-start:var(--cymru-space-6)">
        <li>
            <strong>Not a complete solution today.</strong> The trap root renders as
            <code>&lt;div tabindex="-1"&gt;</code>, which is programmatically focusable but
            not in the tab order. Nothing moves focus there, and <kbd>Tab</kbd> is not
            contained, so this component alone does not meet WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion
            2.4.3 (Focus Order) for modal content.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>RestoreFocus="true"</code> calls
            <code>IFocusManager.RestoreFocusAsync()</code> on disposal. The default
            implementation only logs the call, so focus is not returned to the element
            that was active before the panel opened.
        </li>
        <li>
            For modal content today, use a native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> opened with
            <code>showModal()</code>, or supply your own <code>IFocusManager</code>. Modal
            containers should carry <code>role="dialog"</code>, <code>aria-modal="true"</code>,
            and <code>aria-labelledby</code> pointing to the dialog title.
        </li>
        <li>
            The component does not render its own <kbd>Escape</kbd> handler —
            add a <code>@@onkeydown</code> on the overlay container to close on escape.
        </li>
        <li>
            Real focus movement, restoration and <kbd>Tab</kbd> containment are planned
            for 1.3.0.
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    private bool _trapVisible;

    private void OpenTrap()  => _trapVisible = true;
    private void CloseTrap() => _trapVisible = false;
}
